when talking to college-bound students  it has been quite striking to me how the  notion of financial trade-offs  is so often absent from the  decision-making process  there are indeed reasonable  non-financial factors to consider  but they seem to play an outsized role  students who value aesthetic factors  aren't naive by nature they're simply a  product of a culture that has over  emphasized romantic notions about  college  this culture tends to discourage  aspiring students from being critical  consumers  here's what you can do about that first  use  data to support your decision making and  with those data  compare the benefits you expect from  your degree to the cost for each college  you're considering  finally understand that colleges are  businesses too  and that they still have balance sheets  and bills to pay my point isn't to ruin  the fun of those who feel sentimental  about this important decision  but rather to lessen future regret  weighing the benefits against the cost  is the best way to accomplish that what  factors did you consider  when picking your college let us know in  our poll  also let us know what other topics you'd  like us to cover in 60 seconds  and be sure to subscribe for more  research and videos from aei
 

